    {
      "title": "Tags: Lightweight vs Annotated",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Tags: Lightweight vs Annotated",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Tag Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A tag is a ==fixed, human-readable name== for **one commit**",
                "A branch moves as you commit; a tag ==never moves==",
                "Typical use: label a release, like `v1.0`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Two Kinds",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Lightweight}: `git tag v1.0` is a ref straight at a commit, no metadata",
                "{green:Annotated}: `git tag -a v1.0 -m \"Release 1.0\"` creates a **tag object**",
                "The object stores ==tagger==, ==date==, message and an optional **GPG signature**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Lightweight",
                "Annotated"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Stores",
                  "ref only",
                  "tag object"
                ],
                [
                  "Tagger, date",
                  "{red:none}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`git show`",
                  "commit only",
                  "tag info + commit"
                ],
                [
                  "`git describe`",
                  "ignored by default",
                  "used"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "private temporary marks",
                  "**releases**"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 4
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Releases need -a",
              "text": "A lightweight tag is a bookmark: no author, no date, and `git describe` ignores it by default. Tag every release with ==annotated== tags."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pushing and Managing Tags",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pushing and Managing Tags",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pushing Tags",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git push` does ==not== send tags",
                "One tag: `git push origin v1.0`",
                "All tags: `git push origin --tags`",
                "{blue:Safer}: `git push --follow-tags` sends only ==annotated== tags reachable from pushed commits"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Create, List, Inspect",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git tag -a v0.9 <sha> -m \"msg\"",
                "git tag -l 'v1.*'",
                "git show v1.0"
              ],
              "note": "tag an older commit by giving its sha; -l takes a glob pattern"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Delete a Tag",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Where",
                "Command"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Local",
                  "`git tag -d v1.0`"
                ],
                [
                  "Remote",
                  "`git push origin --delete v1.0`"
                ],
                [
                  "Remote (refspec)",
                  "`git push origin :refs/tags/v1.0`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never move a published tag",
              "text": "`git tag -f` plus a force-push leaves other clones with the ==old tag==. Cut a **new version** (v1.0.1) instead."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Semantic Versioning and git describe",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Semantic Versioning and git describe",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. SemVer Format",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Part",
                "Bump for",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==MAJOR==",
                  "breaking change",
                  "1.5.0 → 2.0.0"
                ],
                [
                  "==MINOR==",
                  "compatible feature",
                  "1.4.2 → 1.5.0"
                ],
                [
                  "==PATCH==",
                  "compatible fix",
                  "1.5.0 → 1.5.1"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A bump ==resets lower numbers== to 0",
                "Pre-release `1.0.0-rc.1` sorts ==before== `1.0.0`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. git describe",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "v1.2.0-5-g3f9a1c2",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "v1.2.0",
                    "note": "nearest annotated tag",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "-5",
                    "note": "commits after the tag",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "-g3f9a1c2",
                    "note": "g + abbreviated hash",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`--tags`",
                  "includes lightweight tags"
                ],
                [
                  "`--always`",
                  "falls back to commit hash"
                ],
                [
                  "`--dirty`",
                  "appends `-dirty` if uncommitted"
                ],
                [
                  "`--abbrev=0`",
                  "prints only the tag name"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes and Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`No names found`: no annotated tag is reachable",
                "Exact tag match prints just the tag, no `-N-g` suffix"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why No names found?** No reachable annotated tag; try `--tags` or `--always`",
                "**What is -5-g3f9a1c2?** 5 commits past the tag, at commit 3f9a1c2",
                "**Breaking change bump?** MAJOR, and MINOR and PATCH reset to 0"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cherry-Pick and Its Conflicts",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cherry-Pick and Its Conflicts",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What It Copies",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git cherry-pick <sha>` copies one commit onto the ==current branch==",
                "The result is a {green:new commit} with a ==new hash==",
                "`-n` applies the changes but does {orange:not commit}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Picks"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`cherry-pick <sha>`",
                  "one commit"
                ],
                [
                  "`cherry-pick A B C`",
                  "several named commits"
                ],
                [
                  "`cherry-pick A^..C`",
                  "==inclusive range== A to C"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Conflicts",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Replays the commit's diff as a ==three-way merge==",
                "Conflicts when the target changed the {red:same lines}",
                "`--abort` abandons the pick; `--skip` drops one commit"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Edit files",
                    "sub": "remove markers",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "git add",
                    "sub": "mark resolved",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "--continue",
                    "sub": "commit is made",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Picking a commit that needs earlier ==unpicked== commits",
                "Picking, then later ==merging the source branch==",
                "The duplicate commit causes confusing conflicts"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A pick is a **copy**, not a link. Git does not remember the original, so a later merge sees two commits."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Backports with cherry-pick -x",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Backports with cherry-pick -x",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Backport with -x",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Backport== = apply a fix from `main` to a maintained release branch",
                "`-x` appends ==(cherry picked from commit <sha>)== to the new message",
                "It records the origin, so the pick is easy to {blue:trace} and audit",
                "{red:Not added by default}; use it only for picks between **public** branches"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git switch release-1.2",
                "git cherry-pick -x 3f9a1c2",
                "git log -1 --format=%B"
              ],
              "note": "the new commit gets a new hash"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "Fix null check in parser",
                "",
                "(cherry picked from commit 3f9a1c2d8e1b)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cherry-pick vs merge",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "cherry-pick",
                "merge"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Brings",
                  "**one** commit",
                  "the **whole** history"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "a fix to backport",
                  "joining branches"
                ],
                [
                  "Risk",
                  "none from other work",
                  "drags in unrelated features"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistake: merge commits",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Merge commit needs -m 1",
              "text": "Picking a merge commit without `-m 1` **fails**. `-m` selects which parent is the ==mainline==; `git cherry-pick -x -m 1 <sha>`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Tags and Patch Transfer",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Tags and Patch Transfer",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Tags and Describe",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git tag v1`",
                  "lightweight tag"
                ],
                [
                  "`git tag -a v1 -m msg`",
                  "annotated tag"
                ],
                [
                  "`git push origin v1`",
                  "push one tag"
                ],
                [
                  "`git push --follow-tags`",
                  "push commits + their annotated tags"
                ],
                [
                  "`git tag -d v1`",
                  "delete locally"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git describe --tags --always --dirty`",
                "Output ==tag-N-gHASH==: N commits after the tag, e.g. `v1.2.0-5-g3f9a1c2`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cherry-pick",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "cherry-pick -x sha",
                    "sub": "copy commit",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Conflict",
                    "sub": "fix files, git add",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "--continue",
                    "sub": "finish pick",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "--abort / --skip",
                    "sub": "give up / drop one",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Patches",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git format-patch -3 -o out/",
                "git format-patch main..HEAD",
                "git am out/*.patch"
              ],
              "note": "one .patch file per commit; -o sets the folder"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git am *.patch`",
                  "commits; keeps author, date, message"
                ],
                [
                  "`git am` conflict",
                  "fix, `git add`, `git am --continue` (or `--abort`)"
                ],
                [
                  "`git apply`",
                  "changes files only, {red:no commit}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`git push` sends no tags. Use ==-x== only between public branches."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You run `git tag -a v1.0 -m \"r\"` then `git push origin main`. Does the remote have v1.0?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No: `git push` of a branch never sends tags.",
                "Run `git push origin v1.0`, or use `--follow-tags`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "HEAD is 3 commits past a lightweight tag `v2.0`, and no annotated tags exist. What does `git describe` do?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It fails: by default it only uses annotated tags.",
                "`git describe --tags` prints `v2.0-3-g` plus the short hash."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`git cherry-pick <merge-sha>` errors out. What is the fix and why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "A merge has two parents, so Git can't tell which diff to replay.",
                "Use `git cherry-pick -m 1 <merge-sha>` to pick the first parent as mainline."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}